[Brian Khuu] And he will be coming back to us to elaborate more about citizen juries and how it's going and its future for over the next decade or so.

64
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:21,760
[Brian Khuu] But in addition, we also have Kimbra White from Mosaiclab.

65
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:27,900
[Brian Khuu] He will also be potentially be able to help us in understanding more about citizen juries as well.

66
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,380
[Alexar Pendashteh?] Any comment?

67
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:32,940
[Alexar Pendashteh?] Because we're lucky to have Kimbra with us today.

68
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:40,100
[Kimbra White] So we've been running citizen juries in Melbourne since 2014.

69
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:48,600
[Kimbra White] Nicholas actually sat in on the first one we did for the 10-year financial plan for the city of Melbourne and wrote a lot about that one that we facilitated.

70
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:51,820
[Kimbra White] We've probably now facilitated over 20 of them.

71
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:54,060
